@format 1
@id section-naming.common.apply-name-state
@title Apply section name change
@section Section naming
@area Common
@entry name-request
@summary Apply a committed section name/prefix/suffix change, synchronously publish and persist it, then classify the information log as naming or renaming from the previously stored main name.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-input, section-naming.pending-inline-commit, section-naming.shortcut-popup
@tag section
@tag split
@tag name
@tag rename
@tag persistence
@tag history

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias history = Cadroue.Application.LHistory
@alias sidecar = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSidecarStore

[name-request] Committed name fields <input>
~ This starts with current name fields.
[Technical explanation]
= A caller supplies a section index plus trimmed main-name, prefix, and suffix values.
> editable-check

[editable-check] Section editing enabled <decision>
~ The program checks section editing enabled.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowNameSet returns immediately when pFlowSectionEditable is false @ flow.PFlowNameSet(...)
? "Editing disabled" > blocked
? "Editing enabled" > index-check

[blocked] Name change blocked <output>
~ This path ends with name change blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= No section state, history, persistence, or naming log changes.

[index-check] Section index valid <decision>
~ The program checks section index valid.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowNameSet reads the current section list and returns when the supplied index is outside it @ flow.PFlowNameSet(...)
? "Index invalid" > invalid
? "Index valid" > capture-old-name

[invalid] Name change ignored <output>
~ This path ends with name change ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section state changes.

[capture-old-name] Capture previous LPieceName <process>
~ The program remembers the section’s previous name.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowNameSet saves the previously stored LPieceName for later log wording, resets pFlowSegmentFired, and calls LSegmentNameSet @ flow.PFlowNameSet(...)
> compare-fields

[compare-fields] Name state differs <decision>
~ The program checks name state differs.
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentNameSet resolves nullable affix arguments and checks whether all three fields are ordinally unchanged using ordinal equality across LPieceName, LPiecePrefix, and LPieceSuffix; if all three match, it returns without applying state @ segment.LSegmentNameSet(...)
? "All three fields unchanged" > unchanged
? "At least one field changed" > replace-piece

[unchanged] No naming mutation <output>
~ This path ends with no naming mutation.
[Technical explanation]
= With no state difference there is no publication or history entry, no sidecar save is attempted, and no naming log is written.

[replace-piece] Replace the indexed LPiece <process>
~ The program replaces the selected section with its renamed version.
[Technical explanation]
- Copy the current section list and replace the indexed piece with the requested main name/prefix/suffix while preserving the current active selection @ segment.LSegmentNameSet(...)
> apply-state

[apply-state] Apply replacement section list <process>
~ This step handles apply replacement section list.
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentApply replaces the internal pieces and synchronously invokes LSegmentChange before attempting persistence @ segment.LSegmentApply(...)
> flow-publish

[flow-publish] Publish renamed section state <process>
~ The section display is updated with the new name.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSegmentHandle sets pFlowSegmentFired, updates Viewfinder and Map section rendering, and synchronously invokes PFlowSectionChange @ flow.PFlowSegmentHandle(...)
> panel-update

[panel-update] Sections panel receives new name fields <process>
~ This step handles sections panel receives new name fields.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionUpdateHandle stores the changed LPiece values/selection and rebuilds the row presentation @ panel.PSectionUpdateHandle(...)
> history-update

[history-update] Workspace history receives the name change <process>
~ This step handles workspace history receives the name change.
[Technical explanation]
- PWorkspaceSectionHandle asks LHistoryAdd to record the workspace snapshot; history-apply mode and an already-identical current state are suppressed @ workspace.PWorkspaceSectionHandle(...)
@ workspace.PWorkspaceHistoryAdd(...)
@ history.LHistoryAdd(...)
> sidecar-save

[sidecar-save] Persist section name fields <process>
~ This step handles persist section name fields.
[Technical explanation]
- After LSegmentChange returns, LSegmentApply calls LSegmentSave; with a source path and outside restore mode, the configured seam writes section records including name, prefix, and suffix @ segment.LSegmentApply(...) / LSegmentSave after LSegmentChange
@ segment.LSegmentSave(...)
@ sidecar.LSidecarSectionsSave(...)
> log-kind

[log-kind] Name or rename wording <decision>
~ The program checks name or rename wording.
[Technical explanation]
- Back in PFlowNameSet, pFlowSegmentFired is true and the wording depends only on the previous LPieceName: empty means named; non-empty means renamed from 'old' to. This classification does not inspect whether only an affix changed @ flow.PFlowNameSet(...)
? "Previous LPieceName empty" > named-log
? "Previous LPieceName non-empty" > renamed-log

[named-log] Record section named <output>
~ This path ends with record section named.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionRecord writes a named information record using the current section state; if only an affix changed while the main name remains empty, the record can still describe the current section itself as unnamed @ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[renamed-log] Record section renamed <output>
~ This path ends with record section renamed.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionRecord writes renamed from 'old-name' to; if only an affix changed while the main name stayed the same, the current implementation still uses rename wording @ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)
